imbridge polls (macOS 26+): send-poll {chatGuid, options, creatorHandle} sends a poll (an iMessage app balloon whose
options travel as base64 JSON in a data: URL inside an archived payload, with the live layout that makes it votable)
and replies with its GUID, sessionIdentifier and optionIdentifiers. send-poll-vote {chatGuid, pollGuid,
sessionIdentifier, participantHandle, optionIdentifiers} casts a vote as a custom acknowledgement of the poll
(associated type 4000) carrying the voter's whole current choice under the poll's own session identifier, after
paging the poll in so IMCore doesn't file the vote elsewhere. Both validate their input and catch exceptions, so bad
input can't crash Messages.

